</section>
<section id="tips" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="tips">Tips</h2>
<ul>
<li>Parameterize the instance type and image URI so the same template works across environments.</li>
<li>Use one stack per environment (dev/staging/prod) rather than branching logic inside a single template.</li>
<li>Tear down with <code>aws cloudformation delete-stack</code> when you’re done — an idle SageMaker endpoint bills by the hour.</li>
</ul>
<p>CloudFormation won’t replace judgment about architecture, but it turns “how did we deploy this?” from a Slack archaeology exercise into a file you can read.</p>


</section>
