<section id="rest-vs-graphql-vs-websocket-in-python" class="level1">
<h1>REST vs GraphQL vs WebSocket in Python</h1>
<p>Most Python backends end up choosing between three communication styles: REST, GraphQL, and WebSocket. They solve different problems, and FastAPI happens to support all three cleanly, which makes it a good way to compare them side by side.</p>
<section id="rest" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="rest">REST</h2>
<p>The default choice for CRUD-style resources. Simple, cacheable, and easy to reason about.</p>
