<section id="when-to-use-which" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="when-to-use-which">When to Use Which</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>REST</strong> — public APIs, CRUD-heavy resources, anything that benefits from HTTP caching.</li>
<li><strong>GraphQL</strong> — nested or variable data shapes, multiple client types (web/mobile) with different needs.</li>
<li><strong>WebSocket</strong> — real-time features like chat, live dashboards, or notifications.</li>
</ul>
<p>They’re not mutually exclusive — a single FastAPI app can serve a REST API, a GraphQL endpoint, and a WebSocket route at once, and it’s common to mix them depending on the feature.</p>


